WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:03.157
Glyph aims to bring AI-accelerated science to

00:03.157 --> 00:04.167
clinical research.

00:04.620 --> 00:07.540
Foundation models may capture new insights into disease

00:07.540 --> 00:11.700
mechanisms from multimodal data, but these signals remain

00:11.700 --> 00:13.280
hidden in dense embeddings.

00:13.820 --> 00:16.460
Glyph exposes them as interpretable concepts.

00:17.400 --> 00:19.983
Distinct neighbourhoods in the concept space reveal patterns

00:19.983 --> 00:21.254
of health and disease.

00:21.880 --> 00:23.293
This creates a playground for discovery.

00:24.480 --> 00:27.105
We can query specific diseases, such as heart

00:27.105 --> 00:29.522
failure, revealing unexpected associations.

00:30.850 --> 00:33.704
Glyph concepts can be combined with existing clinical

00:33.704 --> 00:35.871
research to measure their added benefit.

00:38.180 --> 00:40.618
Choose any disease progression to see whether your

00:40.618 --> 00:43.305
data contains useful risk markers for discovery.

00:43.850 --> 00:44.799
Install Glyph,

00:45.421 --> 00:47.192
or ask Codex or Claude to run it

00:47.192 --> 00:49.483
on your data, and share your own concept

00:49.483 --> 00:51.358
spaces and AI-driven discoveries.
